1
00:00:14,480 --> 00:00:15,793
Ready partner?

2
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:22,280
What are you wearing?

3
00:00:23,087 --> 00:00:24,587
Are you working on a new case?

4
00:00:25,207 --> 00:00:27,347
No, it's an old case.

5
00:00:27,593 --> 00:00:28,800
What do you mean?

6
00:00:34,867 --> 00:00:36,120
Pintu!

7
00:00:36,580 --> 00:00:38,093
What is on the menu today?

8
00:00:41,047 --> 00:00:42,227
Who are these guys?

9
00:00:43,187 --> 00:00:44,593
M...

10
00:00:45,707 --> 00:00:46,800
M?

11
00:00:47,193 --> 00:00:48,320
Who is M, Shekhar?

12
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:50,040
Not Shekhar.

13
00:00:51,547 --> 00:00:52,793
Snehashish.

14
00:01:13,767 --> 00:01:15,620
Who is Chaitali Biswas?

15
00:01:18,860 --> 00:01:20,267
Who is Chaitali Biswas?

16
00:01:21,953 --> 00:01:23,180
Anybody?

17
00:01:25,427 --> 00:01:26,967
Chaitali Biswas,

18
00:01:27,813 --> 00:01:31,147
was the topper in
forensic science last year.

19
00:01:31,680 --> 00:01:33,440
How? Anybody?

20
00:01:34,680 --> 00:01:36,607
-Yes.
-Assignments on time?

21
00:01:36,820 --> 00:01:38,033
-Okay...
-Sir?

22
00:01:38,140 --> 00:01:40,013
100% attendance?

23
00:01:43,207 --> 00:01:44,867
Ladies quota, sir.

24
00:01:48,600 --> 00:01:49,780
Funny man.

25
00:01:50,467 --> 00:01:52,107
Chaitali Biswas...

26
00:01:53,420 --> 00:01:57,346
was the topper because she
was the only student in class...

27
00:01:57,720 --> 00:01:58,648
who passed.

28
00:01:58,673 --> 00:02:01,613
Everyone else failed. She was
number one in the field of one.

29
00:02:01,720 --> 00:02:03,627
So that is Forensic Science.

30
00:02:04,413 --> 00:02:08,045
This... blood, DNA, fingerprints,

31
00:02:08,070 --> 00:02:10,190
can be analysed by any doctor,

32
00:02:10,870 --> 00:02:12,630
but to learn Forensic medicine

33
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:16,527
you need to be an
artist along with a doctor.

34
00:02:17,387 --> 00:02:19,180
Someone who can
see beyond the obvious.

35
00:02:19,493 --> 00:02:23,966
Who can see beyond
what our eyes see.

36
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:26,467
And also look behind what we see.

37
00:02:27,707 --> 00:02:31,313
Like, for example Mr. Hundred Percent
has a stain on the back of his pants.

38
00:02:34,520 --> 00:02:35,833
Let's try it, shall we?

39
00:02:35,950 --> 00:02:37,375
You travel to college
on a two-wheeler, right?

40
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:38,607
Yes sir.

41
00:02:39,270 --> 00:02:40,650
It broke down on the way here.

42
00:02:41,993 --> 00:02:43,680
There was a problem
with the spark plug.

43
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:47,213
Yes sir.

44
00:02:47,287 --> 00:02:49,084
You couldn't find a
mechanic anywhere

45
00:02:49,108 --> 00:02:51,306
and you were getting
late for college so...

46
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:53,747
you decided to do it yourself.

47
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:57,453
He got grease and oil on his hands.

48
00:02:59,393 --> 00:03:01,766
The sleeve on his right hand
was slipping down

49
00:03:01,790 --> 00:03:03,310
so he pulled it up
with his left hand

50
00:03:03,346 --> 00:03:05,193
and on his right hand
he got a little bit of...

51
00:03:06,213 --> 00:03:07,253
grease.

52
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,653
Now he was doing all of
this on the side of the road

53
00:03:10,347 --> 00:03:14,007
of course his pants
are going to get dirty.

54
00:03:14,860 --> 00:03:16,253
It's still dirty, clean it.

55
00:03:16,520 --> 00:03:18,500
Oh no, no my friend.

56
00:03:19,360 --> 00:03:20,593
Just joking.

57
00:03:20,833 --> 00:03:22,340
And... Mr. Funny.

58
00:03:23,793 --> 00:03:26,379
This morning...

59
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:28,446
you had toast for breakfast.

60
00:03:28,867 --> 00:03:30,000
Yes sir.

61
00:03:31,207 --> 00:03:34,373
They become Marxist and grow out
their beards but they don't clean it.

62
00:03:34,573 --> 00:03:35,833
Bread crumbs.

63
00:03:43,827 --> 00:03:44,887
Baabi...

64
00:03:45,187 --> 00:03:46,273
At least listen to me.

65
00:03:47,367 --> 00:03:49,615
What nonsense? How can you say no?
This is a government matter.

66
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:51,693
Exactly! I don't want
to be involved in it.

67
00:03:52,720 --> 00:03:55,253
And definitely not after what
happened last time. I am sorry.

68
00:03:55,733 --> 00:03:57,953
Three bodies, all three scientists
and they all worked at the same place.

69
00:03:58,953 --> 00:04:02,007
Heart attack, suicide, accident.
That too on the same day.

70
00:04:07,287 --> 00:04:10,347
Forensic reports will
take time to come out.

71
00:04:15,550 --> 00:04:16,937
Baabi, I need you.

72
00:04:32,440 --> 00:04:34,027
Sir there are no signs of
a blunt force being used.

73
00:04:34,127 --> 00:04:36,727
We got a random call an hour ago...
We are tracing it...

74
00:04:37,840 --> 00:04:39,180
Shekhar? What is it?

75
00:04:39,327 --> 00:04:40,593
Sudden attack.

76
00:04:41,073 --> 00:04:43,533
Insulin overdose
resulting in hypoglycemia.

77
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:47,073
Her blood sugar dropped so
drastically Bhombol,

78
00:04:47,767 --> 00:04:48,693
that she was dead in 10 minutes.

79
00:04:48,718 --> 00:04:50,007
Really? How?

80
00:04:50,967 --> 00:04:52,467
Didn't you see?

81
00:04:58,753 --> 00:05:00,247
Unbelievable.

82
00:05:00,820 --> 00:05:02,953
No one around here saw the
accident take place!

83
00:05:15,480 --> 00:05:16,633
So,

84
00:05:17,586 --> 00:05:18,906
what do you think?

85
00:05:25,640 --> 00:05:27,353
his hands were tied together first,

86
00:05:28,287 --> 00:05:30,767
Then he was beaten up and the
body was placed here afterwards.

87
00:05:31,833 --> 00:05:32,973
How do you know?

88
00:05:33,213 --> 00:05:34,213
The wrists.

89
00:05:39,440 --> 00:05:40,927
It could have been an accident.

90
00:05:41,187 --> 00:05:44,247
There are no dent marks or scratch
marks created by another car.

91
00:05:44,667 --> 00:05:46,533
There are no skid
marks on the street.

92
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:48,780
Which means he was
completely in control.

93
00:05:49,160 --> 00:05:51,800
This is not an accident, it was
just made to look like one Bhombol.

94
00:06:24,173 --> 00:06:25,580
Bhombol, what is my height.

95
00:06:25,827 --> 00:06:26,805
6' 2.

96
00:06:26,830 --> 00:06:28,845
Yes, and he is 5' 7.

97
00:06:32,507 --> 00:06:35,380
S... S... Snehashish? Snehashish?
What are you doing?

98
00:06:35,405 --> 00:06:36,647
Investigation.

99
00:06:38,560 --> 00:06:39,893
Investigation.

100
00:06:40,913 --> 00:06:43,773
Even if he jumped, his neck
wouldn't reach this noose.

101
00:06:48,700 --> 00:06:50,000
Where do all three work?

102
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,573
Mrinmoy Haldar. Snehashish.

103
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:19,932
Dr. Shanti Nag.

104
00:07:19,957 --> 00:07:22,020
Dr. Sinha is waiting
for you, let's go?

105
00:07:27,053 --> 00:07:31,260
Dr. Sudhir Pandey. Dr. Pramod Prakash.
Prof. Geeta Upadhyay.

106
00:07:31,640 --> 00:07:33,456
We found the dead
bodies of three scientists

107
00:07:33,480 --> 00:07:35,040
from your institute
on the same day.

108
00:07:35,065 --> 00:07:37,067
You can't even imagine
how shocked we are.

109
00:07:37,193 --> 00:07:40,447
As you are aware, we only work
on projects of national importance.

110
00:07:42,813 --> 00:07:44,860
Shanti is our  Liaison Officer.

111
00:07:45,950 --> 00:07:47,870
She is the one who
co-ordinates with the departments.

112
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:50,037
Which departments did
these people work for?

113
00:07:50,553 --> 00:07:51,940
Dr. Pandey was in Pharma.

114
00:07:52,340 --> 00:07:55,913
Prof. Upadhyay worked in Industrial,
and Dr. Prakash was in Environmental.

115
00:07:56,787 --> 00:07:58,800
Were they working on
any project together?

116
00:07:58,833 --> 00:07:59,900
No!

117
00:08:00,533 --> 00:08:02,565
As per safety protocol
at our institute,

118
00:08:02,590 --> 00:08:05,070
there is no direct connection
between departmental operations.

119
00:08:05,393 --> 00:08:08,213
But people can be friends, right?
Did you check that?

120
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:11,560
Every department has its
own cafeterias and rec rooms

121
00:08:11,590 --> 00:08:13,990
most people just interact with
others in their own department.

122
00:08:14,027 --> 00:08:16,507
But honestly... we don't know.

123
00:08:16,587 --> 00:08:19,200
It's a bit difficult to track
everyone's personal lives.

124
00:08:19,300 --> 00:08:21,527
We can easily track personal lives.

125
00:08:22,387 --> 00:08:24,107
Are you having a stroke, Mr. Sinha?

126
00:08:24,287 --> 00:08:26,820
-Snehashish?
-Shallow breathing, dilated pupils,

127
00:08:26,845 --> 00:08:28,587
tiny drops of sweat
on the forehead,

128
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:30,493
of course he is having a stroke. Aren't you?

129
00:08:30,533 --> 00:08:32,208
No, no, every... everything is normal.

130
00:08:32,233 --> 00:08:33,919
Oh, then you must
be hiding something.

131
00:08:34,220 --> 00:08:35,220
What is it?

132
00:08:37,647 --> 00:08:41,747
Sir, we have another
senior scientist,

133
00:08:41,986 --> 00:08:45,887
Dr. Gupta, he hasn't come to
the lab since yesterday either.

134
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:48,300
So you...

135
00:08:49,200 --> 00:08:50,633
were waiting for him to die, right?

136
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:52,393
What? No, no, no...

137
00:08:53,673 --> 00:08:55,940
I didn't want to
create any more panic.

138
00:08:56,430 --> 00:08:58,120
It could have been
a coincidence, right?

139
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:01,193
You have lost three people in
your team. Can't be coincidence.

140
00:09:02,447 --> 00:09:03,973
Have you spoken to Gupta's family?

141
00:09:04,133 --> 00:09:06,160
Actually, Dr. Gupta... you know?

142
00:09:06,240 --> 00:09:08,900
He just takes off every once
in a while. He just disappears.

143
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,947
His wife said the same thing.

144
00:09:11,573 --> 00:09:13,880
It's supposedly a
normal behaviour for him.

145
00:09:14,427 --> 00:09:16,160
I think he will show up soon.

146
00:09:16,185 --> 00:09:18,193
Scientists are crazy.

147
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:20,420
Yeah, yeah they are.

148
00:09:20,660 --> 00:09:22,913
Can we take a look at his
office before he returns?

149
00:09:24,753 --> 00:09:27,220
In fact, can we look
at the offices of all four?

150
00:09:27,620 --> 00:09:28,887
Y... Yes.

151
00:09:30,187 --> 00:09:31,573
Please. Please sir.

152
00:09:31,627 --> 00:09:32,660
Thank you.

153
00:09:35,713 --> 00:09:38,220
He spends more time at the
farmhouse and less time at home.

154
00:09:39,813 --> 00:09:41,355
Is everything alright, sir?

155
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,393
Yes, of course. There is no need to worry.

156
00:09:43,418 --> 00:09:44,698
It's a routine government check.

157
00:09:45,070 --> 00:09:46,702
Will we find him at the
farmhouse right now?

158
00:09:46,727 --> 00:09:48,033
He should be there.

159
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,213
He goes there if
there is too much work.

160
00:09:50,333 --> 00:09:51,480
And what about a phone?

161
00:09:51,787 --> 00:09:54,507
There is no phone there so
I can't get in touch with him.

162
00:09:55,120 --> 00:09:56,387
Otherwise?

163
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:58,127
What?

164
00:09:59,667 --> 00:10:01,047
What if I don't find him there?

165
00:10:01,500 --> 00:10:03,393
If you don't find him there...

166
00:10:03,687 --> 00:10:04,733
Coffee house!

167
00:10:04,758 --> 00:10:05,973
Coffee house?

168
00:10:06,173 --> 00:10:07,680
Coffee house was my
favourite back in college.

169
00:10:12,653 --> 00:10:13,793
What is your name?

170
00:10:14,247 --> 00:10:15,115
Amrita.

171
00:10:15,140 --> 00:10:16,253
Snehashish?

172
00:10:17,893 --> 00:10:19,060
Yeah.

173
00:11:01,373 --> 00:11:02,860
I don't think anyone was here.

174
00:11:04,600 --> 00:11:06,273
-Really?
-I think so.

175
00:11:07,460 --> 00:11:09,113
He must have forgotten
to close the door.

176
00:11:09,260 --> 00:11:11,313
Bhombol you should get a desk job.

177
00:11:12,313 --> 00:11:13,913
Leave the investigating to me.

178
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:17,547
What?

179
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:20,860
These margins of dust
don't match the photo frames.

180
00:11:21,200 --> 00:11:22,473
So someone removed it?

181
00:11:23,240 --> 00:11:24,520
Removed it...

182
00:11:28,747 --> 00:11:31,260
and didn't set it back
properly, clumsy fellows.

183
00:11:39,867 --> 00:11:42,233
Look, this pillow only
has dust on one side.

184
00:11:43,340 --> 00:11:45,373
So someone threw
this on the ground,

185
00:11:45,480 --> 00:11:47,647
looked for something and
then put it back?

186
00:11:48,587 --> 00:11:49,847
Where did he throw it?

187
00:11:50,047 --> 00:11:52,760
-Here... Somewhere...
-No. You're standing on that evidence.

188
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,153
Sorry.

189
00:11:54,267 --> 00:11:55,520
The books have been moved too.

190
00:12:13,900 --> 00:12:15,700
When the mind is without fear,

191
00:12:16,453 --> 00:12:17,800
then the head is held high.

192
00:12:18,753 --> 00:12:21,400
Someone definitely came here to
look for something.

193
00:12:21,793 --> 00:12:23,500
And he searched the
entire house and left.

194
00:12:31,340 --> 00:12:32,413
Baabi?

195
00:12:34,387 --> 00:12:35,493
Where are you going?

196
00:13:28,593 --> 00:13:31,227
You know the pictures of the
offices of all three scientists

197
00:13:32,473 --> 00:13:35,220
that were clicked by
Ashwin and Jadeja,

198
00:13:35,693 --> 00:13:36,960
do you have them?

199
00:13:37,160 --> 00:13:38,340
I do.

200
00:13:55,447 --> 00:13:57,193
Perfect handwriting match.

201
00:13:57,927 --> 00:14:00,193
All four of them working
together on something here.

202
00:14:00,900 --> 00:14:02,207
Not just something Bhombol.

203
00:14:03,400 --> 00:14:04,713
Something dangerous.

204
00:14:12,643 --> 00:14:13,703
Well?

205
00:14:14,167 --> 00:14:16,167
It looks like a list
of raw materials.

206
00:14:16,353 --> 00:14:18,920
It's difficult to say exactly
what they were trying to do

207
00:14:19,833 --> 00:14:21,967
but these are some
highly regulated chemicals,

208
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:25,267
and, if I may say so, harmful too.

209
00:14:26,500 --> 00:14:29,527
-In the wrong hands--
-Three people are dead and one is missing.

210
00:14:30,333 --> 00:14:31,520
Think of the worst doctor.

211
00:14:31,960 --> 00:14:33,367
Yes, but...

212
00:14:33,840 --> 00:14:35,653
These chemicals are
not readily available.

213
00:14:36,827 --> 00:14:40,287
And they can only be bought through
government approved vendors.

214
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:43,693
And you still need a lot of checks
and approvals to get that.

215
00:14:44,270 --> 00:14:46,140
Good. So you have a list of vendors?

216
00:14:47,420 --> 00:14:49,226
They wouldn't buy it through
official channels Bhombol.

217
00:14:51,193 --> 00:14:53,193
They could have bought it
from the Black market, right?

218
00:14:54,513 --> 00:14:56,653
-It's possible.
-If it's possible then...

219
00:14:56,840 --> 00:14:58,040
that is what happened.

220
00:15:03,447 --> 00:15:04,560
Thank you.

221
00:15:17,767 --> 00:15:19,220
-Hello sir.
-Hello sir.

222
00:15:21,800 --> 00:15:23,473
So, what is the conclusion?

223
00:15:24,420 --> 00:15:26,740
The conclusion is that I
don't want to be a part of this.

224
00:15:27,107 --> 00:15:28,480
Oh, serious?

225
00:15:28,527 --> 00:15:29,700
Serious.

226
00:15:30,933 --> 00:15:33,100
You know something. Tell me!

227
00:15:35,513 --> 00:15:37,166
Bhombol, what
department is Pandey in?

228
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:39,033
-Pharma.
-Prakash?

229
00:15:39,733 --> 00:15:40,980
Environmental research.

230
00:15:41,280 --> 00:15:43,027
-Upadhayay?
-She is in Industrial.

231
00:15:43,527 --> 00:15:45,607
And what were their primary papers
during their PhD?

232
00:15:46,307 --> 00:15:49,060
Benzene, Nitrogen, Ethanol.

233
00:15:50,600 --> 00:15:53,527
Do you know what the combination
of the chemicals on your list leads to?

234
00:15:54,267 --> 00:15:55,533
Deadly dangerous.

235
00:15:56,113 --> 00:15:59,473
And Gupta is in Defence,
so the job of weaponizing it...

236
00:15:59,498 --> 00:16:01,240
Was his. Exactly.

237
00:16:01,873 --> 00:16:03,724
Now it is time for my class. Goodbye.

238
00:16:06,200 --> 00:16:07,460
Hey Baabi.

239
00:16:08,927 --> 00:16:11,020
You can't walk away... shit!

240
00:16:11,413 --> 00:16:13,586
Now I remember
Gupta's file said that

241
00:16:13,610 --> 00:16:16,147
he was expelled from
Bardhaman University

242
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,780
because he was experimenting
on an unauthorised chemical.

243
00:16:18,887 --> 00:16:22,100
Exactly, that is why the right to
education is so important Bhombol.

244
00:16:22,727 --> 00:16:24,593
I am going to teach my class.

245
00:16:24,670 --> 00:16:28,470
And besides, now you know why
and how the scientists were killed.

246
00:16:28,820 --> 00:16:30,213
You can handle the rest.

247
00:16:30,547 --> 00:16:31,880
So you definitely won't help me?

248
00:16:32,007 --> 00:16:33,933
I don't want anything
to do with this anymore.

249
00:16:34,747 --> 00:16:36,973
Not even if I tell you
who is behind all this?

250
00:16:44,533 --> 00:16:45,680
Who is?

251
00:16:56,720 --> 00:16:57,887
M!

252
00:16:58,287 --> 00:17:00,640
A dangerous
international arms dealer.

253
00:17:01,653 --> 00:17:04,640
Nobody knows who he is or
where he is from.

254
00:17:07,880 --> 00:17:12,393
Some say that he is
Ex-KGB, Ex-RAW, or Ex-ISI...

255
00:17:15,390 --> 00:17:16,515
We don't know...

256
00:17:16,540 --> 00:17:18,595
We don't even know
whether it's he or she.

257
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:20,900
Is he a myth? Or a ghost?

258
00:17:22,247 --> 00:17:23,367
No one has ever...

259
00:17:30,900 --> 00:17:32,167
No one has ever seen him.

260
00:17:33,373 --> 00:17:35,046
But everyone knows that this person

261
00:17:35,070 --> 00:17:37,466
sets up shop in conflict
zones all over the world.

262
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:39,060
Cambodian Civil War,

263
00:17:39,187 --> 00:17:41,607
Angolan War, Burma Conflict...

264
